    "skyPreset": "golden_alpine_meadow",
    "loreSummary": "The port road clips Grykefell's north-east corner and stops for nothing: no village stands on the region, no track branches off, and the working coast is the whole width of the region away on the west side. So the ground is taken off the water instead \u2014 a hull in the lagoon behind the bar, block stone off the benches where the sea has planed the pavement flat, ore out of the cave the swell drove along a seam in that same rock, and water carried down from the sink inland."
  },
